<title>GERMANY: Bankgesellschaft details 1996 earnings.</title>
<headline>Bankgesellschaft details 1996 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    355    vs 958</p>
<p>    Group net profit			    47     vs 476</p>
<p>    Group oper profit before provisions   1,775  up 5.6 pct</p>
<p>    Dividend (proposed)			 1.10   vs 1.10 dmk</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total		 337,500 up 19.9 pct</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 3,697  vs 3,501</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     685    vs 628</p>
<p>    Group own-account trading income	74     vs 87</p>
<p>    DVFA earnings per share (marks)  3.07 loss   vs 2.47 profit</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Bankgesellschaft Berlin AG. The bank already reported operating profit after provisions, group net profit, operating profit before provisions and the dividend proposal on Friday.</p>
<p>The group comprises Landesbank Berlin, Berliner Bank and mortgage unit Bank Berlin Hyp. It is 56.8 percent-owned by the state of Berlin while Norddeutsche Landesbank holds a 19.6 percent stake.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
